      ]
    },
    {
      "ribbon": {
        "icon": "snippet",
        "label": "Paragraph 2 •0:38 "
      }
    },
    {
      "text": [
        {
          "images": [
            {
              "position": "right",
              "src": "/assets/images/extras/audiobooks/starter/young-learners-adults/the-troy-stone/paragraph-2.avif",
              "alt": "Paragraph 2 image"
            }
          ],
          "blocks": [
            {
              "block": [
                {
                  "text": "There are forty people on the bus. They come from Britain, America, France, Italy and Holland. At Troy they all have lunch. Then they start to look at the old city. It is a very hot day. After an hour, Mark sits under a tree. “I’m going to stop here for a moment,” he tells Fay. “OK,” she answers. Then, Mark sees something on the ground. “What’s that?” he thinks."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "exercises": [
        {
          "title": "1.1 Fill in the blank with the correct answer."
        },
        {
          "fillExercises": [
            {
              "card": false,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "block": [
                    {
                      "text": "1.1 ...",
                      "correctAnswer": ["..."]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "..."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ribbon": {
        "icon": "snippet",
        "label": "Paragraph 3 • 1:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": [
        {
          "images": [
            {
              "position": "right",
              "src": "/assets/images/extras/audiobooks/starter/young-learners-adults/the-troy-stone/paragraph-3.avif",
              "alt": "Paragraph 3 image"
            }
          ],
          "blocks": [
            {
              "block": [
                {
                  "text": "It is a flat, yellow stone. Mark picks it up. Then he starts to clean it with his hands. “But I know this stone,” he thinks. “It comes from... from...” Suddenly, there is a white light in his eyes. Mark closes them. The light is strong. Now there is a loud wind in his ears. He cannot hear or see anything. ”What’s happening ?” he thinks."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "exercises": [
        {
          "title": "1.1 Fill in the blank with the correct answer."
        },
        {
          "fillExercises": [
            {
              "card": false,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "block": [
                    {
                      "text": "1.1 ...",
                      "correctAnswer": ["..."]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "..."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ribbon": {
        "icon": "snippet",
        "label": "Paragraph 4 • 2:00"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": [
        {
          "images": [
            {
              "position": "right",
              "src": "/assets/images/extras/audiobooks/starter/young-learners-adults/the-troy-stone/paragraph-4.avif",
              "alt": "Paragraph 4 image"
            }
          ],
          "blocks": [
            {
              "block": [
                {
                  "text": "Ten seconds later the light and the wind stop. Mark opens his eyes. He is standing on a beach. He can see hundreds of ships and men. Behind him there is a beautiful city with high walls. “Where am I?” he thinks. “Where’s my family?” He puts the yellow stone in his pocket. Then one of the men says to him, “Boy! Come here!”"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "exercises": [
        {
          "title": "1.1 Fill in the blank with the correct answer."
        },
        {
          "fillExercises": [
            {
              "card": false,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "block": [
                    {
                      "text": "1.1 ...",
                      "correctAnswer": ["..."]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "..."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ribbon": {
        "icon": "snippet",
        "label": "Paragraph 5 • 2:36"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": [
        {
          "images": [
            {
              "position": "right",
              "src": "/assets/images/extras/audiobooks/starter/young-learners-adults/the-troy-stone/paragraph-5.avif",
              "alt": "Paragraph 5 image"
            }
          ],
          "blocks": [
            {
              "block": [
                {
                  "text": "“Me?” Mark walks across the beach to a long, black ship. “Carry this,” the man says. He gives Mark a lot of wood. Then he gets off the ship. “Follow me,” he says. Mark follows him. The man is very tall and has a short, brown beard. “I don’t know your face,” he says. “Are you new here?” “Yes,” Mark answers. “That’s right. I’m new here.”"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "exercises": [
        {
          "title": "1.1 Fill in the blank with the correct answer."
        },
        {
          "fillExercises": [
            {
              "card": false,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "block": [
                    {
                      "text": "1.1 ...",
                      "correctAnswer": ["..."]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "..."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ribbon": {
        "icon": "snippet",
        "label": "Paragraph 6 • 3:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": [
        {
          "blocks": [
            {
              "block": [
                {
                  "text": "“My name is Andros,” says the man. He and Mark walk for another ten minutes. Then they climb a small hill. At the top Mark stops. There, in front of them, is a big wooden horse. Andros sees Mark’s face and smiles. “Well... what do you think of it?” he asks. Mark does not answer, and Andros says, “This horse is going to win the war for us Greeks.”"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
